# Architecture and scope

- The architecture and structuer is detail explained in the /docs, it should be keeped as it is described after every change.

- **`src/app/`**: App shell only—`App`, `providers`, `routes`, route-level pages and layouts. No HTTP clients, env reads, or low-level utils here.
- **`src/core/`**: `api` (including `apiClient`), `config`, shared domain/backend `types`, global Zustand stores. No reusable UI components.
- **`src/shared/`**: Reusable `components`, `hooks`, `utils`, `constants`. Re-export from local `index.ts` when it improves imports.
- **`src/contexts/`**: One concern per file—provider + matching `useX` hook (e.g. `useThemeMode`, `useLanguage`).
- **`src/theme/`**, **`src/i18n/`**: Theme and i18n only; no business logic. Theme may include **`produzaTokens.ts`** / **`mui-augment.ts`** used exclusively by **`createAppTheme`** to expose **`palette.produza`**—features consume tokens via **`useTheme()`**, not local token files.

Prefer **`src/features/<name>/`** when a product area grows (auth, settings, etc.); keep `app/routes` thin by importing feature pages.

# Imports

- Use the **`@/`** alias for all `src` imports (see `vite.config.ts`). Avoid deep relative paths like `../../../core/...`.

# Agent behavior

- Do not add code comments unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not add `console.log`; use existing logging patterns if any (`console.warn` / `console.error` only where ESLint allows).
- Reuse existing `shared` and `contexts` patterns before adding new abstractions.
- Keep changes minimal and scoped to the request—no drive-by refactors.

User-facing copy: keys and locale files stay aligned with app types (e.g. `AppLanguage` in `LanguageContext`).
